Subject: Load extensions with RTLD_DEEPBIND under Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

PHP 8.5 stopped passing RTLD_DEEPBIND to dlopen() where dlmopen() exists.
Fil-C exports the functions that libraries built with -fvisibility=hidden
keep internal natively, so an extension's library then binds them to the
first library in the global scope that has the same name. The sodium
extension's one-shot BLAKE2b (sodium_crypto_generichash(), the KDF, key
exchange and Argon2i) called libargon2's blake2b_update(), which PHP links,
with libsodium's state, and hashed the empty string whatever its input.
Restore PHP 8.4's behaviour.

--- a/Zend/zend_API.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_API.c
@@ -41,7 +41,17 @@
 /* these variables are true statics/globals, and have to be mutex'ed on every access */
 ZEND_API HashTable module_registry;
 
+#ifdef __FILC__
+/* Fil-C exports functions a library built with -fvisibility=hidden meant to
+ * keep internal, so without RTLD_DEEPBIND an extension's library can bind
+ * them to another library's functions of the same name: libsodium's BLAKE2b
+ * called libargon2's blake2b_update, which PHP itself loads, and hashed
+ * nothing. Keep binding each library to its own symbols first, as PHP did
+ * before 8.5. */
+ZEND_API bool zend_dl_use_deepbind = true;
+#else
 ZEND_API bool zend_dl_use_deepbind = false;
+#endif
 
 static zend_module_entry **module_request_startup_handlers;
 static zend_module_entry **module_request_shutdown_handlers;
